---
<BaseLayout title="Boba, Bingsu and Other Sweets — Huanyu Chen"
  description="Drinks and desserts, 2022–2026, region by region: boba in the San Gabriel Valley, Los Angeles and Orange County, a summer in the Bay Area, and a few on the road, each with a map of the shops.">
  <p class="muted"><a href="/misc">← Misc</a> · 2022 – 2026</p>
  <h1>Boba, Bingsu and Other Sweets</h1>
  <p class="muted trip-sub">The drinks and desserts we keep going back for, and a few we only had once.</p>

  <div class="callout trip-stats">
    <strong>4 years · July 2022 – November 2026</strong><br />
    a galaxy-blue boba and a brown-sugar one · HEYTEA in New York and Molly Tea after dark · two lattes, one lavender ·
    bingsu with bananas, with mango and with strawberries · matcha soft serve and purple shave ice · Porto's, Crumbl and a
    dozen from Krispy Kreme · a Genshin cup at Happy Lemon
  </div>

  <p>
    This is the sweet half of what we eat out. Meals will get their own post. Drinks and desserts are the bigger habit:
    by a rough count, the tea shops, coffee bars and bakeries in this post add up to several hundred visits over four
    years, far more than any restaurant.
  </p>
  <p>
    The post goes region by region, each with a map of the shops in it. A chain shows every branch we went to in that
    region; it is rarely more than two. The photos come from both of our phones, most of the drinks from my wife's
    camera roll, held up in one hand in front of the shop, the car dashboard or the next table.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sgv">San Gabriel Valley</h2>
  <p>
    Most of the boba is here, on Valley Boulevard in Alhambra and San Gabriel, where the tea shops line up one after
    another for a couple of miles.
  </p>
  <RegionMap stores={SGV} region="the San Gabriel Valley" />
  <p>
    On July 7, 2022 it was <strong>Xing Fu Tang</strong>, where the brown sugar boba is cooked in a wok at the counter,
    and a drink in a deep galaxy blue. Ten days later there was a crawl down East Valley Boulevard that ended at
    <strong>3 Cats Tea</strong> (三喵制茶), with a row of drinks lined up under the shop's cat figurines.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'xingfutang-galaxy.webp'} alt="A deep blue boba drink in a domed plastic cup on a counter." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Xing Fu Tang, Alhambra, July 7, 2022.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'three-cats-row.webp'} alt="Four tea drinks lined up on a white counter under a shelf of small cat figurines." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>3 Cats Tea, San Gabriel, July 17, 2022.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    The regulars since then are a short list within a few blocks of each other: <strong>Chicha San Chen</strong>,
    <strong>Alittle Tea</strong>, <strong>MeloMelo</strong>, and <strong>Cotti</strong>, whose cups come with cartoon
    characters.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'chicha.webp'} alt="A hand holding a cup of milk tea with a paper sleeve." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Chicha San Chen, San Gabriel, March 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'cotti.webp'} alt="A hand holding two iced drinks with cartoon cups." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Cotti, San Gabriel, January 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    MeloMelo's drinks come piled with whipped cream and fruit. A little north, <strong>Fika Fika</strong> in Arcadia makes
    lattes in two colors, plain and lavender.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'melomelo.webp'} alt="Two fruit drinks topped with whipped cream next to a small jar, on a green table." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>MeloMelo, San Gabriel, March 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'fika.webp'} alt="Two iced lattes, one plain and one lavender, on a wooden table." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Fika Fika, Arcadia, June 2023.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    The newest obsession is <strong>Molly Tea</strong> (茉莉奶白), the jasmine milk tea chain. Its first Los Angeles shop
    opened on Valley Boulevard in spring 2025, with a giant pink cup surrounded by flowers out front.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'molly-cup.webp'} alt="A giant pink Molly Tea cup reading Oriental Jasmine, surrounded by white and pink flowers on a patio." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The giant cup outside Molly Tea, San Gabriel, April 25, 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    Nine days later there was a line out the door well after ten at night. Down the same street, <strong>Yu Cake</strong>
    makes mille crêpe cakes; this slice is from October 2025.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'molly-queue.webp'} alt="A line of people outside a lit tea shop at night, seen from behind." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The line at Molly Tea, May 4, 2025, 10:20 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'yu-cake.webp'} alt="A slice of layered crêpe cake on a white plate." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Yu Cake, October 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="la">Los Angeles</h2>
  <p>
    The rest of Los Angeles is more spread out: Century City, Little Tokyo and Koreatown, the blocks around USC,
    Glendale and Burbank, and Torrance in the South Bay.
  </p>
  <RegionMap stores={LA} region="Los Angeles" />
  <p>
    <strong>HEYTEA</strong>'s Los Angeles shop and <strong>Chamberlain Coffee</strong> sit almost next to each other in
    Century City. Chamberlain makes a purple drink with a flower on top. In Little Tokyo, <strong>SomiSomi</strong> fills a
    fish-shaped waffle with soft serve.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'chamberlain.webp'} alt="A purple iced drink topped with a yellow flower." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Chamberlain Coffee, Century City, April 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'somisomi.webp'} alt="A hand holding a fish-shaped waffle cone filled with soft serve, in front of a SomiSomi shop." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>SomiSomi, Little Tokyo, June 2024.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    Fall 2022 was around Little Tokyo and USC: koala-face cones with cookie ears, and teddy-bear parfaits.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'koala-cones.webp'} alt="Two hands holding ice-cream cones decorated as koala faces with cookie ears." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Koala cones, Little Tokyo, October 2022.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'teddy-parfaits.webp'} alt="Two parfait cups decorated as teddy bears, one strawberry and one blueberry." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Teddy-bear parfaits, near USC, September 2022.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    Before Christmas 2024 there was a trip to the <strong>Krispy Kreme</strong> on Crenshaw, where the donuts come off the
    line onto racks behind the glass, and a dozen came home.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'krispy-racks.webp'} alt="Racks of glazed and filled donuts behind a glass counter." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Krispy Kreme, Crenshaw, December 19, 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'krispy-dozen-r.webp'} alt="A box of a dozen assorted donuts." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The dozen.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    <strong>Porto's</strong> is the bakery we visit most, in Glendale and Burbank, for the cake case as much as anything.
    The matcha soft serve is from the food court at the <strong>Mitsuwa</strong> market in Torrance.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'portos-case.webp'} alt="A glass bakery case full of whole cakes." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The cake case at Porto's, Glendale, October 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'mitsuwa-matcha.webp'} alt="A swirl of green matcha soft serve in a black cup." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Matcha soft serve, Mitsuwa, Torrance, January 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    And two smaller ones: mango sticky rice from <strong>Kanomwaan</strong> in Thai Town, and in September 2024 the
    <em>Genshin Impact</em> meal at McDonald's, whose apple pie came in a box with the game's logo.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'mango-sticky-rice.webp'} alt="Mango slices over sticky rice with coconut sauce in a takeout box." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Mango sticky rice, Kanomwaan, Thai Town, April 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'mccafe-pie.webp'} alt="A yellow McCafé baked apple pie box with a green Genshin Impact emblem." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>McDonald's Genshin meal, September 2024.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="oc">Orange County</h2>
  <p>
    In Orange County the list is mostly cafés and dessert shops rather than tea. The exception is <strong>HEYTEA</strong>,
    which the card records show more often than any other tea shop, at its two shops in Irvine.
  </p>
  <RegionMap stores={OC} region="Orange County" />
  <p>
    <strong>Sul &amp; Beans</strong> in Irvine is the bingsu place: shaved milk ice piled in a bowl and topped with sliced
    banana and cream, or with strawberries, or with mango and toasted coconut.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'sul-banana.webp'} alt="A bowl of shaved ice topped with banana slices, crumbs and cream." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Banana bingsu, Sul &amp; Beans, Irvine, April 2025.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'sul-strawberry.webp'} alt="Two bingsu bowls, one with strawberries and one with mango and coconut, on a wooden table." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Strawberry and mango, May 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    <strong>Coffee Dose</strong> in Costa Mesa puts its drinks in pastel cups. <strong>Crumbl</strong> is a pink box of
    oversized cookies, here a strawberry one.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'coffee-dose.webp'} alt="A hand holding a pastel blue and pink iced drink in a car." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Coffee Dose, Costa Mesa, December 2025.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'crumbl-strawberry.webp'} alt="A large cookie topped with cream and fresh strawberries in a pink box." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Crumbl, Costa Mesa, March 2026.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    <strong>Salt &amp; Straw</strong> is usually a cup to go. And on November 1, 2025 there were croissants at
    <strong>Chaupain Bakery</strong>, with Wangcai sitting very politely next to the box.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'salt-straw.webp'} alt="A cup of pale green ice cream with chocolate pieces." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Salt &amp; Straw, Newport Beach, October 2026.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'chaupain-wangcai.webp'} alt="A white dog sitting next to a box of croissants on an outdoor table." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Chaupain Bakery, Newport Beach, November 1, 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    In November 2024 <strong>Happy Lemon</strong> in Tustin did a <em>Genshin Impact</em> collab, with life-size
    standees of Klee and Kirara by the door and a themed cup and bag.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'happylemon-standee.webp'} alt="Cardboard standees of two anime characters inside a photo frame at a tea shop." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Happy Lemon × Genshin, Tustin, November 17, 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'happylemon-cup.webp'} alt="A hand holding a drink in a Genshin-themed cup next to a matching paper bag." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The cup and the bag.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    The counter was covered in merchandise. And one more bingsu, strawberry, at <strong>Heybings Desserts &amp; Coffee</strong> in Irvine in January 2026.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'happylemon-counter.webp'} alt="A shop counter covered with Genshin-themed menus, bags and a plush figure." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The counter at Happy Lemon.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'sulbing-strawberry.webp'} alt="A strawberry bingsu on a metal tray with a fan of sliced strawberries." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Strawberry bingsu, Heybings, Irvine, January 2026.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="bay">Bay Area</h2>
  <p>
    From June to August 2026 the Bay Area got a short list of its own, mostly along El Camino Real.
  </p>
  <RegionMap stores={BAY} region="the Bay Area" />
  <p>
    In Santa Clara, a matcha latte from <strong>Big Mug Coffee Roaster</strong>, and a few doors down at
    <strong>Sulbing</strong> a mango bingsu with a scoop of ice cream on the very top.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'matcha-big-mug.webp'} alt="A hand holding a bright green iced matcha latte in a parking lot." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Big Mug Coffee Roaster, Santa Clara, June 2026.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'sulbing-mango.webp'} alt="A large bowl of shaved ice covered in mango cubes and cheesecake, with a scoop of ice cream on top." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Mango bingsu, Sulbing, Santa Clara, July 6, 2026.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    In August there was a flight at <strong>The Coffee Movement</strong> in San Francisco, a latte and three small glasses
    on a ledge with the street behind.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig narrow-fig"><img src={P + 'coffee-movement.webp'} alt="A latte and three small glasses of coffee on a ledge, with a San Francisco street behind." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The Coffee Movement, San Francisco, August 2026.</figcaption></figure>

  <h2 id="away">On the road</h2>
  <p>
    New York gets its own map, because both of the big tea chains followed us there.
  </p>
  <RegionMap stores={NY} region="New York" />
  <p>
    At the end of July 2024, on the summer road trip, it was <strong>HEYTEA</strong> by Times Square two days running: a
    yellow fruit tea one evening, and the next afternoon a cup held up in front of the sign.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'heytea-yellow.webp'} alt="A hand holding a yellow fruit tea in front of a wall of menu screens." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>HEYTEA, Times Square, July 29, 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'heytea-store.webp'} alt="A hand holding a milk tea with a black cartoon logo, in front of a HEYTEA shop sign." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The next afternoon, July 30.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    Two years later, in July 2026, it was <strong>Molly Tea</strong> on the Upper West Side.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig narrow-fig"><img src={P + 'molly-drinks.webp'} alt="Two milk teas, one with a pink question-mark logo, on a counter." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Molly Tea, New York, July 31, 2026.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    And the rest, scattered across the map: <strong>Rare Tea</strong> outside Seattle in July 2023, rolled ice cream in
    Santa Barbara, a Molly Tea in Philadelphia, and shave ice on the Big Island.
  </p>
  <RegionMap stores={AWAY} region="other trips" />
  <p>
    Rare Tea came in paper bags. In Santa Barbara, on a sunny June day, Wangcai sat on guard beside the table.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'rare-tea.webp'} alt="Two boba drinks, one brown and one pink, in branded paper bags." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Rare Tea, Kirkland, July 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'rolled-wangcai.webp'} alt="A white dog sitting by a patio table with a cup of rolled ice cream." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Rolled ice cream and Wangcai, Santa Barbara, June 28, 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    On the Big Island in September 2026 it was shave ice: purple and white under a cap of cream, with a striped straw, and
    the next afternoon a bowl crowned with an orchid.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'shave-ice.webp'} alt="A cup of purple and white shave ice topped with cream, with a red-striped straw." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Original Big Island Shave Ice Co., Waikoloa, September 8, 2026.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'shave-ice-bowl.webp'} alt="A bowl of shave ice topped with fruit, coconut flakes and a pink orchid." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The next day, with an orchid.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="shuffle">Shuffle</h2>
  <p>
    And everything else: 648 drinks and desserts from my wife's camera roll, one from each outing, in a random
    order that changes every time the page loads.
  </p>
  <Album base={P + 'album/'} list={ALBUM} subject="a drink or dessert" />

  <p class="muted"><small>Photo locations have been removed from the published images. Map pins mark the shops themselves,
    mostly from OpenStreetMap. Visit counts come from our own records and only count the times we paid by card.</small></p>
  <Comments />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .trip-sub { margin-top: -.4em; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .trip-stats { margin: 1.2em 0; line-height: 1.6; }
  .trip-fig { margin: 1.2em 0; }
  .trip-fig img { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; display: block; }
  .trip-fig figcaption { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; margin-top: .35em; text-align: center; }
  .narrow-fig { max-width: 420px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .trip-pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 12px; align-items: start; }
  .trip-pair .trip-fig { margin: .6em 0; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .trip-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
